SOURCE-AVAILABLE, NOT OPEN SOURCE
=================================

This repository is public so the work can be read, learned from, and
discussed. It is NOT released under an open-source licence, and that is a
deliberate choice rather than an oversight.

WHY NOT MIT OR APACHE
---------------------
This repository contains third-party assets - fonts, icons, art and audio -
that are licensed TO this project by their creators. Those licences do not
grant the right to sub-license. Applying an open-source licence to this
repository would purport to grant you rights over material the copyright
holder does not hold, which would be wrong regardless of intent.

The credits screen in the game lists every third-party asset and its creator.
If you want to use one of them, licence it from its creator directly.


WHAT YOU MAY DO WITHOUT ASKING
------------------------------
- Read, study and learn from this source.
- Quote portions of the code in reviews, tutorials, articles or teaching
  material, with attribution.
- Download, install and play the released builds on devices you control.
- Record, stream, and monetise video of the game. You do not need permission
  and you do not owe a revenue share.
- Report bugs, request features, and open pull requests.

WHAT REQUIRES PERMISSION
------------------------
- Redistributing this source or the builds, in whole or in substantial part.
- Publishing a modified build, or presenting any build as an official release.
- Selling the game, or charging for access to it.
- Extracting assets for use in other projects. Most of them are not ours to
  give; see above.

Ask, and the answer is usually yes for anything non-commercial.


SCRIPTURE
---------
The scripture text in this game is drawn from translations in the public
domain. It is not our property, we claim no rights over it, and nothing in
this licence restricts your use of it. Any future translation used under
licence would be governed by that licence rather than this one.


